<p dir="auto">We have the qualifier "HTML attribute:" on attribute pages (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Attributes/accept" rel="nofollow">example</a>), but it is missing from titles for global attributes.<br>
This PR adds "HTML global attribute:" to the <code class="notranslate">title</code> key and repurposes the existing title as <code class="notranslate">short-title</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">To ensure consistency in title format in the same technology area. This also benefits SEO.</p>]]></content>
